    "created_at": "2018-03-28T10:34:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-28T10:34:45Z",
    "body": "In Live DOM Viewer:\r\n```html\r\n<img>\r\n<script>\r\nonload = function() {\r\n  var img = document.querySelector('img');\r\n  img.addEventListener(\"x\", () => document.open());\r\n  img.addEventListener(\"x\", w);\r\n  img.dispatchEvent(new Event(\"x\"));\r\n};\r\n</script>\r\n```\r\nlogs the event in Firefox and Safari, but not in Chrome. Hurray, edge case found another minor interoperability issue.\r\n\r\nAnyone want to make an argument here one way or another?\r\n\r\n@foolip @cdumez @smaug---- ",
